{"actor":{"id":"claude-fable-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_012HDu8WZMnLiywxEiECv4Jm","input":{"content":"---\nname: evintunador-workflow-preferences\ndescription: How the user wants Claude to work — subagents for economy, intent questions before building\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nThe user asked (2026-07-19) to save context window and subscription rate\nlimits by delegating to sub-agents of lesser models (haiku/sonnet) where\napplicable, and to ask clarifying questions about their *intent* before\nbuilding — they expect the right questions to significantly shift the design,\nand they answer them thoughtfully (often via the \"Other\" free-text option).\n\n**Why:** they are on a rate-limited subscription and treat the main-model\ncontext as a scarce resource; they also treat design docs as provisional and\nexpect intent to be re-derived through dialogue rather than followed blindly.\n\n**How to apply:** fan out exploration/research/format-reverse-engineering to\nbackground haiku/sonnet agents in parallel; keep the main context for\nsynthesis, decisions, and precision coding. Before implementing a new\nproject, present findings and ask 3-4 sharp intent questions\n(AskUserQuestion) whose answers change the architecture. Related:\n[[turnbridge-mvp-decisions]].\n","file_path":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-turnbridge/memory/evintunador-workflow-preferences.md"},"name":"Write","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"326b8177b0e7a698f5508e341c37244044cfdbe2afc06b333559e99d10b54f75","head":"db72655e67a3005a5585eb09e9faf6c5169bad5d","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":509},"id":"ev1-2945fb10a4e659fdb7d5016472d2948c6fb16a24fb869ae109a819e4857741db","kind":"conversation_turn","occur