{"actor":{"id":"claude-fable-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01N9zvY7DTLiJG7e9cuKXHF2","input":{"questions":[{"header":"Ownership","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"description":"Turnbridge = picker + rehydration on top of cledger's existing capture. MVP effort goes entirely into the novel part; capture adapters stay in conversation-ledger (docs get updated to match reality).","label":"Resume layer only (Recommended)"},{"description":"Refactor: ledger becomes pure neutral storage per its product intent; Turnbridge takes over the claude-code/codex adapters, hooks, and cursoring. Cleaner boundaries, but today is mostly a code-move day.","label":"Move adapters into Turnbridge"},{"description":"Turnbridge is the user-facing product that wraps/vendors cledger entirely (install, capture, resume, sync all behind one `turnbridge` command). Users never learn cledger exists.","label":"Ledger is an internal detail"}],"question":"conversation-ledger already implements incremental capture for Claude Code and Codex (hooks, transcript parsers, cursors, dedup). Turnbridge's docs say Turnbridge owns the adapters. Given capture is essentially done, what is Turnbridge actually?"},{"header":"Rehydration","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"description":"Launch a fresh target session whose first prompt/context is the canonical transcript (or a file + 'read this'). Labeled as rehydrated. Format-drift-proof, matches your docs.","label":"Honest bootstrap (Recommended)"},{"description":"Write a target-native JSONL session file so `claude --resume`/`codex resume` natively sees the conversation. Seamless UX, but version-pinned and breaks silently when formats change.","label":"Native session fabrication"},{"description":"Bootstrap is the guaranteed path; fabrication is an opt-in flag per target CLI where the format is known-good. More MVP surface area.","label":"Both, bootstrap default"}],"question":"For rehydrating a conversation into the other CLI, which mechanism should the MVP use? Your docs mandate honest 'new session + transcript bootstrap' and treat writing fabricated provider-native session files as an optional risky extra — but the competitors (authsec-bridge, cross_agent_session_resumer) bet on native fabrication because the UX is seamless."},{"header":"Primary user","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"description":"You hit Claude rate limits mid-task and continue in Codex (or vice versa), same machine, same repo. Sharing/team features stay out of the MVP entirely.","label":"Solo dev hopping CLIs"},{"description":"A teammate picks up your conversation on their machine via the git-notes sync. Requires sync UX, author labels, redaction concerns much earlier.","label":"Team handoff"},{"description":"The durable ledger for intent-recall is the real product; cross-CLI resume is a demo/secondary feature. Prioritizes capture completeness and schema over resume UX.","label":"Evidence record first"}],"question":"Who is the MVP for? The inspirations pull in different directions: SpecStory/competitors serve a solo dev hopping CLIs; sticky-note is team handoff between humans; intent-recall wants a durable evidence record."},{"header":"CLI UX","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"description":"`turnbridge resume` (or `tb`) shows one merged picker of compatible conversations from both CLIs, then launches native resume or rehydration. No shimming; zero risk of breaking normal `claude`/`codex` usage.","label":"Standalone command (Recommended)"},{"description":"Per your design doc: a wrapper named `claude`/`codex` earlier in PATH that intercepts `--resume` and shows the merged picker, delegating everything else. Slicker, but PATH games and CLI-flag drift make it fragile for day one.","label":"Shim intercepting --resume"},{"description":"Build the picker as `turnbridge resume` today with the internals structured so the shim is a thin wrapper we add once the picker is proven.","label":"Standalone now, shim later"}],"question"