{"actor":{"id":"claude-fable-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"The MVP is built and working end-to-end. All 10 tasks are complete: 6 turnbridge tests + 46 conversation-ledger tests pass, and both cross-CLI fabrication directions were verified against the real binaries — a fabricated Codex rollout resumed via `codex exec resume` and a fabricated Claude session via `claude --resume`, each correctly recalling planted facts from the imported history. `turnbridge list` in this repo already shows this very conversation (your cledger hooks captured it live).\n\n**What exists now**\n\n- **turnbridge** (this repo, TypeScript, zero runtime deps beyond conversation-ledger): `turnbridge resume [claude|codex]` — merged picker filtered to conversations compatible with the current repo/HEAD and authored by you (`--all` for collaborators, `--any-commit` for other branches); same-CLI picks delegate to native resume; cross-CLI picks fabricate a target-native session file and hand off to the target's own resume; `--bootstrap` (and automatic fallback) does honest transcript rehydration; first target pick offers to save a default; `turnbridge shim install` is the opt-in `claude --resume` interceptor.\n- **Upstream conversation-ledger changes** (uncommitted there too): a library entry point (`exports`/`main`/`types` + `src/index.ts`), and human turns now stamped with `actor.id`/`display` from git `user.email`/`user.name` — the identity your sharing model filters on. One caveat documented in its design doc: a forced full transcript rescan can duplicate pre-identity events, since `actor.id` participates in the event-id hash.\n- **Version-pinned format specs** in `docs/specs/` (claude 2.1.215, codex-cli 0.144.6), empirically derived by the research agents from your real session files with fabricate-and-resume experiments. Notable findings baked into the adapters: Claude's resume walks `parentUuid` links backward from the last line and is scoped to the project dir encoded from