{"actor":{"type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Your questions have been answered: \"conversation-ledger already implements incremental capture for Claude Code and Codex (hooks, transcript parsers, cursors, dedup). Turnbridge's docs say Turnbridge owns the adapters. Given capture is essentially done, what is Turnbridge actually?\"=\"Resume layer only (Recommended)\", \"For rehydrating a conversation into the other CLI, which mechanism should the MVP use? Your docs mandate honest 'new session + transcript bootstrap' and treat writing fabricated provider-native session files as an optional risky extra — but the competitors (authsec-bridge, cross_agent_session_resumer) bet on native fabrication because the UX is seamless.\"=\"both, native session fabrication default, bootstrap as an optionally triggerable last-resort for when formats change and cause buggy behavior\", \"Who is the MVP for? The inspirations pull in different directions: SpecStory/competitors serve a solo dev hopping CLIs; sticky-note is team handoff between humans; intent-recall wants a durable evidence record.\"=\"MVP is me dev hopping CLIs AND me sharing chats with my collaborators, who also like to dev hop CLIs, such that they and i can choose wehtehr to only see our own chats or optionally also each others'. a big reason the hopping CLIs feature is so necessary for the sharing/collaboration part is because _different people use different CLIs_. i assume cledger already shares git usernames or something that we can build off of, no?\", \"What should the MVP's command surface be?\"=\"standalone & shim now, standalone default, shim optionally turned on. eventually shim may become default of we observe that it's pretty consistent over the course of a few weeks. also, do i understand correctly the `turnbridge resume` will show u the list of convos and then let u choose which to open it in? may something like `turnbridge resume codex` would mean that when you select your version you go straight to codex without the CLI asking u, or maybe u can set a default one to open in. yooo like maybe first time u go into it and u choose a chat to open and it asks which cli u want to resume it in, it also asks if u want to make ur choice the default.\". You can now continue with these answers in mind.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01N9zvY7DTLiJG7e9cuKXHF2","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"326b8177b0e7a698f5508e341c37244044cfdbe2afc06b333559e99d10b54f75","head":"db72655e67a3005a5585eb09e9faf6c5169bad5d","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":87},"id":"ev1-135f7510522128d245509664050cf1171705c9bcd6eb69d3ac06c0d83d75bcad","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-19T06:54:57.277Z","producer":{"session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","source":"claude-code","tool":"cledger","version":"0.1.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"Your questions have been answered: \"conversation-ledger already implements incremental capture for Claude Code and Codex (hooks, transcript parsers, cursors, dedup). Turnbridge's docs say Turnbridge owns the adapters. Given capture is essentially done, what is Turnbridge actually?\"=\"Resume layer only (Recommended)\", \"For rehydrating a conversation into the other CLI, which mechanism should the MVP use? Your docs mandate honest 'new session + transcript bootstrap' and treat writing fabricated provider-native session files as an optional risky extra — but the competitors (authsec-bridge, cross_agent_session_resumer) bet on native fabrication because the UX is seamless.\"=\"both, native session fabrication default, bootstrap as an optionally triggerable last-resort for when formats change and cause buggy behavior\",