bricated provider-native session files as an optional risky extra — but the competitors (authsec-bridge, cross_agent_session_resumer) bet on native fabrication because the UX is seamless."},{"header":"Primary user","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"description":"You hit Claude rate limits mid-task and continue in Codex (or vice versa), same machine, same repo. Sharing/team features stay out of the MVP entirely.","label":"Solo dev hopping CLIs"},{"description":"A teammate picks up your conversation on their machine via the git-notes sync. Requires sync UX, author labels, redaction concerns much earlier.","label":"Team handoff"},{"description":"The durable ledger for intent-recall is the real product; cross-CLI resume is a demo/secondary feature. Prioritizes capture completeness and schema over resume UX.","label":"Evidence record first"}],"question":"Who is the MVP for? The inspirations pull in different directions: SpecStory/competitors serve a solo dev hopping CLIs; sticky-note is team handoff between humans; intent-recall wants a durable evidence record."},{"header":"CLI UX","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"description":"`turnbridge resume` (or `tb`) shows one merged picker of compatible conversations from both CLIs, then launches native resume or rehydration. No shimming; zero risk of breaking normal `claude`/`codex` usage.","label":"Standalone command (Recommended)"},{"description":"Per your design doc: a wrapper named `claude`/`codex` earlier in PATH that intercepts `--resume` and shows the merged picker, delegating everything else. Slicker, but PATH games and CLI-flag drift make it fragile for day one.","label":"Shim intercepting --resume"},{"description":"Build the picker as `turnbridge resume` today with the internals structured so the shim is a thin wrapper we add once the picker is proven.","label":"Standalone now, shim later"}],"question":"What should the MVP's command surface be?"}]},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"32d4ef56-474c-4243-9229-c251