member, JSONL format with tool_use entries\n- **Presence tracking**: `.sticky-note/presence/{username}.json` — active files per developer\n- **Signal files**: `.sticky-resume`, `.sticky-session`, `.sticky-head` (local only, git-ignored) for session continuity and resume coordination\n\n**Transcript Parsing:**\n- `parse-transcript.js` handles both JSONL (Claude Code transcript) and plaintext (fallback)\n- Extracts narrative: last assistant message (300 char max)\n- Detects failed approaches: combines ERROR_PATTERNS regex + RETRY_PATTERNS to identify error→retry sequences\n- Handles tool_use entries to extract files touched from tool inputs\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Supported CLIs &amp; Transcript Formats**\n\n| CLI | Format | Discovery | Resume |\n|-----|--------|-----------|--------|\n| **Claude Code** | JSONL transcript + hook input | SessionStart/SessionEnd hooks (per-session) | `.sticky-resume` signal file + `resume-thread` CLI |\n| **Copilot CLI** | Reconstructed from audit trail (no direct transcript access) | `sessionStart`/`sessionEnd` per turn + hook env vars | Same as Claude Code, works cross-CLI |\n| **Codex** | Plaintext stdout/stderr captured via bash wrapper | Post-session `sticky-codex.sh` wrapper | Via MCP server only |\n| **MCP Clients** (Cursor, Windsurf, etc.) | N/A — read-only via 8-tool MCP server | Via `get_thread_context_for_files()` MCP tool | Via `get_session_context()` MCP tool |\n\n**Key discovery mechanisms:**\n- `sticky-note.json` stores all threads with full metadata\n- `.sticky-note/audit/*.jsonl` provides session-level detail\n- `git blame` integration for file→thread attribution (V2.5+)\n- `resume-thread --query \"topic\"` does text similarity search across narratives/failed_approaches\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Directly Reusable Code**\n\n**parse-transcript.js** (67 lines) — Production-ready transcript extraction:\n- Handles JSONL + plaintext formats\n- ERROR_PATTERNS &amp; RETRY_PATTERNS regex for failed approach detection\n- Exports `extractNarrativeFromEntries()`, `extractFailedFromEntries()` \n\n**sticky-utils.js** (1,132 lines) — Comprehensive session utilities:\n- Path resolution (`getMemoryPath()`, `getAuditDir()`)\n- JSON I/O with git merge strategy (`saveMemoryMerged()`)\n- Thread search &amp; filtering (`findThreadById()`)\n- Audit trail querying (`extractSessionFromAudit()`)\n- Git blame integration for attribution\n\n**sticky-attribution.js** (534 lines) — File→thread mapping:\n- Runs `git blame --line-porcelain` per file\n- Three-tier SHA resolution (Git Notes → Audit JSONL → file+date heuristic)\n- Returns line ranges for context injection\n\n**bin/mcp-server.js** (partial) — Inter-tool communication:\n- 8 MCP tools: `get_session_context()`, `search_threads()`, `check_overlaps()`, `get_thread_context_for_files()`\n- Zero external dependencies\n- Stdio JSON-RPC 2.0 protocol\n\n**session-end.js capture logic** (1,021 lines):\n- Extracts files touched from transcript tool_use entries + git diff\n- Classifies work type via activity patterns\n- Computes resume_chain for cross-tool continuity\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Tech Stack &amp; Maturity**\n\n- **Language**: Node.js &gt;= 16 (pure JS, no TypeScript)\n- **Dependencies**: Zero — uses only Node.js built-ins (fs, path, child_process, crypto)\n- **Storage**: Git repository (branch-independent via orphan branch in v3.0.0)\n- **Data format**: JSON for threads, JSONL for audit logs\n- **Size**: ~6,300 lines of hook code across 12 files\n- **Maturity**: Actively maintained, v3.0.0 recent (data-branch refactor), 50+ commits in last cycle\n- **Testing**: Smoke test suite exists\n\n**Architecture decisions relevant to Turnbridge:**\n- Avoids external service: Everything stored locally in git\n- CLI-agnostic thread format: Same data structure works across Claude Code, Copilot CLI, Codex\n- Multi-layer context injection: Static instructions + per-session + per-prompt + MCP tools gives resilience if one channel fails\n- Git merge strategy: `.gitattributes merge=union` + UUID threads avoid conflicts on concurrent pushes</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>49338</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>25</tool_uses><duration_ms>92739</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"326b8177b0e7a698f5508e341c37244044cfdbe2afc06b333559e99d10b54f75","head":"db72655e67a3005a5585eb09e9faf6c5169bad5d","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":79},"id":"ev1-db8445f49aeb39b417d6dace57376d00f3a18452ae9dca732e73240317f4dc88","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-19T06:36:51.335Z","producer":{"session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","source":"claude-code","tool":"cledger","version":"0.1.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a264be797d1ae6615</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01MXwCMdXhxP15onNoqgUbAa</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-turnbridge/c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e/tasks/a264be797d1ae6615.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Explore sticky-note repo\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Sticky-note Exploration Report\n\n### 1. **Purpose**\nSticky-note is **git-backed shared memory for human-to-human handoff between AI coding assistants**. It captures what happens in each session (files touched, work type, narrative, failed approaches) and surfaces this context to teammates automatically on their next session—making implicit knowledge explicit without changing how anyone works. Currently at v3.0.0, MIT licensed, ~6.3K lines of Node.js hook code.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Architecture Overview**\n\n**Session Capture Pipeline:**\n- **Hooks at lifecycle events**: `SessionStart` → `SessionEnd` (Claude Code) or `sessionStart` → `sessionEnd` per turn (Copilot CLI)\n- **Per-prompt injection**: `UserPromptSubmit`/`userPromptSubmitted` scores open threads by relevance (file overlap, branch match, recency)\n- **Tool tracking**: `PostToolUse` appends JSONL audit entries (file, tool name, session ID) for every tool call\n- **Error capture**: `PostToolUseFailure` marks threads as stuck and records failed approaches\n\n**Data Storage:**\n- **Thread state**: `.sticky-note/sticky-note.json` (git-tracked) — one JSON object with `threads[]` array, each with ID, user, status, files_touched, narrative, failed_approaches, resume_chain, contributors\n- **Per-user audit logs**: `.sticky-note/audit/{username}.jsonl` — one file per team member, JSONL format with tool_use entries\n- **Presence tracking**: `.sticky-note/presence/{username}.json` — active files per developer\n- **Signal files**: `.sticky-resume`, `.sticky-session`, `.sticky-head` (local only, git-ignored) for session continuity and resume coordination\n\n**Transcript Parsing:**\n- `parse-transcript.js` handles both JSONL (Claude Code transcript) and plaintext (fallback)\n- Extracts narrative: last assistant message (300 char max)\n- Detects failed approaches: combines ERROR_PATTERNS regex + RETRY_PATTERNS to identify error→retry sequences\n- Handles tool_use entries to extract files touched from tool inputs\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Supported CLIs &amp; Transcript Formats**\n\n| CLI | Format | Discovery | Resume |\n|-----|--------|-----------|--------|\n| **Claude Code** | JSONL transcript + hook input | SessionStart/SessionEnd hooks (per-session) | `.sticky-resume` signal file + `resume-thread` CLI |\n| **Copilot CLI** | Reconstructed from audit trail (no direct transcript access) | `sessionStart`/`sessionEnd` per turn + hook env vars | Same as Claude Code, works cross-CLI |\n| **Codex** | Plaintext stdout/stderr captured via bash wrapper | Post-session `sticky-codex.sh` wrapper | Via MCP server only |\n| **MCP Clients** (Cursor, Windsurf, etc.) | N/A — read-only via 8-tool MCP server | Via `get_thread_context_for_files()` MCP tool | Via `get_session_context()` MCP tool |\n\n**Key discovery mechanisms:**\n- `sticky-note.json` stores all threads with full metadata\n- `.sticky-note/audit/*.jsonl` provides session-level detail\n- `git blame` integration for file→thread attribution (V2.5+)\n- `resume-thread --query \"topic\"` does text similarity search across narratives/failed_approaches\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Directly Reusable Code**\n\n**parse-transcript.js** (67 lines) — Production-ready transcript extraction:\n- Handles JSONL + plaintext formats\n- ERROR_PATTERNS &amp; RETRY_PATTERNS regex for failed approach detection\n- Exports `extractNarrativeFromEntries()`, `extractFailedFromEntries()` \n\n**sticky-utils.js** (1,132 lines) — Comprehensive session utilities:\n- Path resolution (`getMemoryPath()`, `getAuditDir()`)\n- JSON I/O with git merge strategy (`saveMemoryMerged()`)\n- Thread search &amp; filtering (`findThreadById()`)\n- Audit trail querying (`extractSessionFromAudit()`)\n- Git blame integration for attribution\n\n**sticky-attribution.js** (534 lines) — File→thread mapping:\n- Runs `git blame --line-porcelain` per file\n- Three-tier SHA resolution (Git Notes → Audit JSONL → file+date heuristic)\n- Returns line ranges for context injection\n\n**bin/mcp-server.js** (partial) — Inter-tool communication:\n- 8 MCP tools: `get_session_context()`, `search_threads()`, `check_overlaps()`, `get_thread_context_for_files()`\n- Zero external dependencies\n- Stdio JSON-RPC 2.0 protocol\n\n**session-end.js capture logic** (1,021 lines):\n- Extracts files touched from transcript tool_use entries + git diff\n- Classifies work type via activity patterns\n- Computes resume_chain for cross-tool continuity\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Tech Stack &amp; Maturity**\n\n- **Language**: Node.js &gt;= 16 (pure JS, no TypeScript)\n- **Dependencies**: Zero — uses only Node.js built-ins (fs, path, child_process, crypto)\n- **Storage**: Git repository (branch-independent via orphan branch in v3.0.0)\n- **Data format**: JSON for threads, JSONL for audit logs\n- **Size**: ~6,300 lines of hook code across 12 files\n- **Maturity**: Actively maintained, v3.0.0 recent (data-branch refactor), 50+ commits in last cycle\n- **Testing**: Smoke test suite exists\n\n**Architecture decisions relevant to Turnbridge:**\n- Avoids external service: Everything stored locally in git\n- CLI-agnostic thread format: Same data structure works across Claude Code, Copilot CLI, Codex\n- Multi-layer context injection: Static instructions + per-session + per-prompt + MCP tools gives resilience if one channel fails\n- Git merge strategy: `.gitattributes merge=union` + UUID threads avoid conflicts on concurrent pushes</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>49338</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>25</tool_uses><duration_ms>92739</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","role":"user"},"origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"parentUuid":"1679ec43-559e-43f9-ba52-a00e11b015f3","permissionMode":"auto","promptId":"15f410f0-3bfe-4c16-af92-5ae00d138044","promptSource":"system","sessionId":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","slug":"generic-stirring-candy","timestamp":"2026-07-19T06:36:51.335Z","type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"7275a16c-5cea-4737-adf8-2ec2b82d6515","version":"2.1.215"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-07-19T07:14:51.665Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
{"actor":{"type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a49750c41a1d47ca5</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_0173D4kkTo2sotrSWjmyHdbY</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-turnbridge/c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e/tasks/a49750c41a1d47ca5.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Explore intent-recall sibling\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Intent Recall Exploration Report\n\n**Purpose:**\nIntent Recall is an evidence-backed retrieval system designed to help humans and AI agents find historical proof of intended behavior in repositories. It inspects recorded conversations, decisions, specifications, code, and tests to answer \"what behavior was actually intended?\" The system distinguishes original requests from later changes of mind and exposes underlying evidence with full provenance, treating each implementation artifact as a lossy expression of human goals.\n\n**Relationship to Conversation Ledger &amp; Turnbridge:**\nIntent Recall is fundamentally a **consumer** of Conversation Ledger data. It reads immutable events directly from the shared ledger to build derived, versioned indexes. Turnbridge is explicitly identified as \"one valuable producer of conversational evidence,\" but Intent Recall is designed to support decisions arriving through multiple ingestion paths—not exclusively Turnbridge. This establishes a clear division:\n- **Turnbridge**: Captures CLI session transcripts as conversation events in Conversation Ledger\n- **Intent Recall**: Reads from Conversation Ledger (plus other evidence sources) to retrieve and structure intent evidence\n\nThe systems share the Conversation Ledger as their data model bridge.\n\n**Design Constraints on Conversation Event Storage:**\n\n1. **Immutability &amp; Addressability**: All events must be immutable with permanent event IDs, allowing raw evidence to remain directly addressable. Derived indexes reference exact event IDs and excerpts.\n\n2. **Evidence Granularity**: An open design question is source-link granularity—should citations point to turns, paragraphs, sentences, or spans? This directly affects how fine-grained conversation events need to be segmented.\n\n3. **Metadata Requirements**: Each conversational event should support:\n   - Chronological ordering and timestamping\n   - Actor identification (who made requests/decisions)\n   - Explicit supersession relationships (when later events override earlier ones)\n   - Contradiction detection and tracking\n\n4. **Structured Claims over Raw Conversations**: While raw conversations are preserved, Intent Recall derives structured annotations tracking actors, requested behaviors, constraints, acceptance criteria, scope, and supersession. Each derived claim requires source links, confidence scores, and extractor/version provenance.\n\n5. **Distinction Between Evidence Types**: The model classifies evidence as:\n   - Human requests and clarifications\n   - Accepted/rejected decisions and their chronology\n   - Specifications and documentation\n   - Tests and code (treated as implementation artifacts, not unquestioned intent)\n\nThis means conversation events should preserve conversational context richly enough to retroactively classify whether a message represents a human request, decision ratification, or clarification.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>11052</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>6</tool_uses><duration_ms>21628</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"db72655e67a3005a5585eb09e9faf6c5169bad5d","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677